  "limitations": [
    "All runtime scenarios are NOT_EXECUTED; no COBOL compiler, loader, database, or model is used.",
    "Call contexts denote bounded static callsite chains, not reachable paths or chronological executions.",
    "The two shared-worker contexts reuse one source callsite and one static symbol; only context-qualified field identities separate them.",
    "No ancestor values or automatic transitive writebacks are asserted. CONTENT blocks writes back to the original root request.",
    "Program WORKING-STORAGE can persist across invocations; context labels alone do not prove separate runtime storage.",
    "ON EXCEPTION and ON SIZE ERROR are source clauses, not a complete exception control-flow graph.",
    "PAIRJOIN's defensive size-error arm is not proven reachable within the declared input layouts.",
    "Main excludes boundaries; negative cases are indexed separately."
  ]
